{"id":774,"date":"2020-11-04T11:47:05","date_gmt":"2020-11-04T19:47:05","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=774"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:41:36","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:41:36","slug":"conditionals-2","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/conditionals-2\/","title":{"rendered":"2C: Conditionals"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22167de390a\" name=\"6a22167de390a\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What are if statements?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If statements are conditionals, which are used to help your program make decisions. You actually use conditionals every day! Some examples might include:<\/span><\/p>\n<ol>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If my alarm goes off, then I will wake up. Else, I will stay asleep.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If I am hungry, I will eat something.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If it&#8217;s sunny out, I will wear sunscreen.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If my room is clean, I will get my allowance. Else, I will make no money.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If statements in Python are written like this:<\/span><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">if insert condition here:\r\n\r\n     Insert statements here\r\n\r\nelse:\r\n\r\n     Insert statements here<\/pre>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">See what they look like in our example:<\/span><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">if alarm goes off:\r\n\r\n     I will wake up\r\n\r\nelse:\r\n\r\n     Stay asleep<\/pre>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The condition is what the computer checks to know if it is true or false.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If the condition is true, the computer will execute the statements underneath it.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If the condition is false, the computer will NOT execute the statements underneath it.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u201cElse\u201d has no condition. This is because \u201celse\u201d is the last option when using if-else statements.\u00a0 When a computer reaches the \u201celse\u201d option after checking all the other conditions, the else condition is automatically true and will run its statements.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">One way to use \u201celse\u201d would be when something needs to happen when a condition is false. When the if condition is false and nothing needs to happen, you don\u2019t need to use an \u201celse\u201d.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22167de3a5c\" name=\"6a22167de3a5c\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Indentation<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Indentation is very important in Python. The indentations indicate which statements belong to a particular section in the code.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You may have noticed that the statements below the if and else statements are indented <\/span><b>4 spaces<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> or one <\/span><b>tab<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. If you want to have multiple statements executed if a condition is true using proper indentation, it would look like this:<\/span><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">if battery_percentage &gt; 60:\r\n\r\n    print(\"Ready for takeoff!\")\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0drone.takeoff()\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0drone.land()\r\n\r\nelse:\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0print(\"Battery too low.\")<\/pre>\n<p>Below is an incorrect example. Try running it to see what happens. Your goal: correct the example by indenting correctly and fixing the syntax.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">drones = 100\r\n\r\nbugs = 55\r\n\r\nif drones &gt; bugs print(\"Squish the bugs!\")\r\n\r\nelse print(\"Fly away!\")<\/pre>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The example should look something like this. Try running it now and change the values of drones and bugs.<\/span><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">drones = 100\r\n\r\nbugs = 55\r\n\r\nif drones &gt; bugs:\r\n\r\n    print(\"Squish the bugs!\")\r\n\r\nelse:\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 print(\"Fly away!\")<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22167de3af9\" name=\"6a22167de3af9\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Comparators<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In the last few steps, you were introduced to a new symbol. The &gt; sign is an example of a <\/span><b>comparator<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, but you may know it as an inequality sign from math class. Comparators can be used inside conditions to<\/span> compare values<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. If the statement is true, the statement below will execute. These are comparators:<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&gt; Greater than<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&lt; Less than<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&gt;= Greater than or equal to<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&lt;= Less than or equal to<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">== Equal to<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">!= Not equal to<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Here&#8217;s an example that uses them. Try it out for yourself! Run the code without changing the values, then change X and Y so that the sum is equal to 50. You can also try changing the comparator to see what happens!<\/span><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">import CoDrone_mini\r\n\r\nfrom CoDrone_mini import Direction\r\n\r\ndrone = CoDrone_mini.CoDrone()\r\n\r\ndrone.pair()\r\n\r\nX = 10\r\n\r\nY = 30\r\n\r\nif X + Y == 50:\r\n\r\n    print(\"Correct, X + Y is equal to 50.\")\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0drone.takeoff()\r\n\r\ndrone.flip(Direction.Forward)\r\n\r\ndrone.land()\r\n\r\nelse:\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0print(\"Incorrect.\")<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22167de3b80\" name=\"6a22167de3b80\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Programming assignment<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Create 3 variables with different numerical values. Next, write at least 3 if statements and an else statement. Use the variables as the conditions for the if statements. The statements of the if statements and else statement should print different strings. The program below is an example &#8212; try writing your own!<\/span><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">import CoDrone_mini\r\ndrone = CoDrone_mini.CoDrone()\r\ndrone.pair()\r\n \r\nx = 58\r\ny = 12\r\nz = 90\r\n \r\ndrone.takeoff()\r\nif x &gt; y:\r\n   drone.set_pitch(50)\r\n   drone.move(2)\r\nif z &gt; x:\r\n   drone.set_roll(50)\r\n   drone.move(2)\r\nif y+z &gt; x:\r\n   drone.set_yaw(50)\r\n   drone.move(2)\r\nif y &gt; z:\r\n   drone.set_throttle(50)\r\n   drone.move(2)\r\nelse:\r\n   drone.land()\r\n<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22167de3bfe\" name=\"6a22167de3bfe\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What are else if statements?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Pretend that you have two buttons: one button opens a door, and the other button closes the door. You also have code that will check if the buttons are pressed. Your first thought might be to write something like this:<\/span><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">if button 1 is pressed:\r\n\r\n    Close the door\r\n\r\nif button 2 is pressed:\r\n\r\n    Open the door<\/pre>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">What happens if you press both at the same time? Both are true and the door would try to open and close at the same time!<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Else if statements, written as <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">elif<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> in Python, solve this problem. Once a condition is met, the code will not execute any of the other elif statements, whether they are true or not. Just like an if statement, if the code runs through all of the conditions and none are met, then the else statement will execute. Although you don&#8217;t need an else statement, it&#8217;s usually a good idea to include one to handle any errors or unexpected cases. Here is an adjusted code using elif.<\/span><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">if button 1 is pressed:\r\n\r\n    Close the door\r\n\r\nelif button 2 is pressed:\r\n\r\n    Open the door<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22167de3c8a\" name=\"6a22167de3c8a\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Rollercoaster Challenge<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This challenge will be checking if a person is tall enough to ride a rollercoaster. <\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You\u2019ll declare a variable called \u00a0<code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">height<\/code>\u00a0<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, which will represent height in inches. <\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The height should be checked at 48 and 36. <\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Anyone under 36 inches is not allowed to ride. <\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Riders between 36 and 48 inches can ride with a parent. <\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Riders above 48 inches can ride alone.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;2846&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Add the drone in by having it throttle up for 3 seconds at 48 inches and above and at 2 seconds for 36-48 inches. For any variable under 36 inches, it should yaw for 1 second.<\/span><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">import CoDrone_mini\r\n\r\ndrone = CoDrone_mini.CoDrone()\r\n\r\ndrone.pair()\r\n\r\n\r\nheight = 66\u00a0 # height in inches\r\n\r\ndrone.takeoff()\r\n\r\n\r\nif height &gt; 48:\r\n\r\n    drone.set_throttle(50)\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 drone.move(3)\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 print(\"Rider can ride alone\")\r\n\r\nelif height &gt; 36:\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 drone.set_throttle(50)\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 drone.move(2)\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 print(\"Rider must be accompanied by parent\")\r\n\r\nelse:\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 drone.set_yaw(50)\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 drone.move(1)\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 print(\"Rider not allowed on the ride\")\r\n\r\ndrone.land()<\/pre>\n<p>drone.close()[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 7 What are if statements? [vc_column_text]If statements are conditionals, which are used to help your program make decisions. You actually use conditionals every day! Some examples might include:&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/conditionals-2\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1730,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":744,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1782,1848,1793,1826,1482,853,694,59,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2135,2125,2119,2123,2122,2134],"class_list":["post-774","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-beginner","lesson-tag-codrone-mini","lesson-tag-conditionals","lesson-tag-fundamentals","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-python","module-beginner","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/774","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":5,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/774\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":2847,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/774\/revisions\/2847"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1730"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=774"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=774"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=774"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}